Z||000004||WGraffiKs||03-27-2000||03:08 AM||||I'm not too keen on the idea, but, hey, if you want one, make sure it leaves enough clearance to lift the rear decklid all the way up without hitting!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||03-27-2000||10:52 AM||||I know there use to be 2 kinds for the Fiero. One was against the window and the other was at an angle that met the pillars. The angled one had two rails that taped to the decklid so when you opened the back it swung up along the rails. I had this type on my first fiero and took them off a week later. I didn't like how they operated. You almost had to grease the rails for smooth operation and the 2-sided tape didn't hold to well on hot days. Cleaning the back window or washing the car was a pain also. You had to undo the top hinge clips and lay it on the wing to get the area that was covered. I finally just took them off and sold them to someone else.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-27-2000).]||||reg||13
